					"patching_rect" : [ 15.0, 196.0, 689.0, 100.0 ],
					"text" : "Voices whose clef spans multiple staff stilll bear an initial rule by default to highlight the fact that they are a single voice.\nHowever, you can now change this type of shape by tweaking the \"multistaffaccollatura attribute\".\n\nShapes include: \"none\" (no shape), \"rule\" (line), \"thinbracket\" (a thin bracket), \"bracket\" (the standard musical bracket), and \"brace\" (the usual piano-staff brace). \n\nIn particular, this makes it possible to have piano-like curly brackets (\"brace\")."
